 it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\n# Loop poll intervals. Unset loops keep their defaults (scanners 4h, triage\n# 15m, workers 5m, reviewers 5m, prwatch 5m); 1m is the minimum. Hand-offs\n# no longer wait for a poll: a close-out wakes the next loop, a freed slot\n# wakes loops with waiting work, and approvals and unblocks are watched every\n# minute (#394, #406). The merger is controller code with no agent or job\n# slot, so it polls every minute to merge green PRs sooner.\nintervals: { merger: 1m }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make lint test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\ninternal/config/defaults.go:264:// LabelRunes counts s the way GitHub limits label names: in characters.\ninternal/servecmd/observe.go:10:// it records the usage windows of an agent step in the limits book, for a\ninternal/servecmd/observe.go:12:// limits.observe_failed and never fails the job.\ninternal/servecmd/observe.go:22:\tb, err := o.w.limitsBook(ctx)\ninternal/servecmd/observe.go:27:\t\to.w.Log.Warn(\"limits.observe_failed\", \"error\", err)\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:19:\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/limits\"\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:114:\t\tClassify: reaper.UsageLimitClassifier(w.Model.Auth), Limits: lazyLimits{w}, Readings: readingObserver{w}}\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:123:// lazyLimits is the Finisher's LimitRecorder. The book opens on first use (the\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:126:type lazyLimits struct{ w *wiring }\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:128:func (l lazyLimits) Exhaust(ctx context.Context, family string, resetsAt time.Time) (time.Time, error) {\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:129:\tb, err := l.w.limitsBook(ctx)\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:136:func (l lazyLimits) Succeeded(ctx context.Context, family string) error {\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:137:\tb, err := l.w.limitsBook(ctx)\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:144:// limitsBook returns the one limits book of this process, opened on first use.\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:147:func (w *wiring) limitsBook(ctx context.Context) (*limits.Book, error) {\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:153:\tb, err := limits.Open(ctx, w.Store, time.Now, w.Log)\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:162:// given the usage limits recorded so far. Deterministic scanners use no model\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:193:\treturn book.Until(limits.FamilyOf(role.Model))\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:217:\tif _, err := w.limitsBook(ctx); err != nil {\ninternal/servecmd/scanners.go:57:\t\t\tLimits: func() scanner.LimitRecorder {\ninternal/servecmd/scanners.go:58:\t\t\t\tb, err := w.limitsBook(context.Background())\ninternal/servecmd/scanners.go:61:\t\t\t\t\tw.Log.E